1
00:00:03,570 --> 00:00:06,206
- Next, detach the celiac artery.
- Yes.

2
00:00:07,240 --> 00:00:08,708
You are holding the wrong part.

3
00:00:09,776 --> 00:00:10,610
Sorry.

4
00:00:12,479 --> 00:00:15,115
- Double ligature on right gastric artery.
- Yes.

5
00:00:18,618 --> 00:00:20,520
I said the right gastric artery.

6
00:00:20,587 --> 00:00:22,756
Not left! What are you doing?

7
00:00:22,822 --> 00:00:23,757
Okay.

8
00:00:23,823 --> 00:00:25,525
- Hold the forceps.
- What?

9
00:00:25,592 --> 00:00:28,128
- You idiot!
- Sorry.

10
00:00:28,194 --> 00:00:30,463
Dr. Daimon, calm down.

11
00:00:30,897 --> 00:00:33,199
Blood pressure 110/70,
heart rate 90.

12
00:00:33,266 --> 00:00:36,336
I'll do it. You do the blood suction.

13
00:00:36,403 --> 00:00:38,004
- Sorry, I'm sweating.
- Okay.

14
00:00:38,071 --> 00:00:40,774
- You didn't do anything. Don't sweat.
- No, ma'am.

15
00:00:41,274 --> 00:00:42,876
- You're in my way.
- Sorry.

16
00:00:42,942 --> 00:00:44,277
Cut the suture.

17
00:00:44,344 --> 00:00:45,245
Give me a mayo.

18
00:00:45,311 --> 00:00:47,881
TSUKASA AYUKAWA, INTERN

19
00:00:48,748 --> 00:00:49,783
Don't pick it up!

20
00:00:50,116 --> 00:00:52,886
Do not use the dropped tool, idiot!

21
00:00:53,286 --> 00:00:54,320
Oh, I see.

22
00:00:54,387 --> 00:00:57,424
You all just stand behind.

23
00:00:57,490 --> 00:00:58,658
That's correct.

24
00:00:58,725 --> 00:00:59,559
- Scalpel.
- Yes.

25
00:01:05,865 --> 00:01:09,069
How carefree the freelancer can be.

26
00:01:09,135 --> 00:01:12,272
All she has to do is perform surgery.

27
00:01:12,338 --> 00:01:15,675
We shouldn't care for the outsider.

28
00:01:15,742 --> 00:01:19,579
About this report's credibility
and confidentiality?

29
00:01:19,646 --> 00:01:21,881
- Not to worry.
- We treat it with extra care.

30
00:01:21,948 --> 00:01:24,918
We're taking about it
in this closed-room.

31
00:01:25,285 --> 00:01:27,020
Nobody can eavesdrop on us.

32
00:01:28,388 --> 00:01:29,956
Spectators,

33
00:01:30,523 --> 00:01:32,725
help us if you have time
to observe us.

34
00:01:32,792 --> 00:01:34,294
Those interns are helpless.

35
00:01:34,360 --> 00:01:37,964
Why does the freelancer
have to train interns?

36
00:01:39,165 --> 00:01:43,236
As I thought, I'm not popular
in the internal medicine department.

37
00:01:43,303 --> 00:01:44,237
POPULARITY REPORT

38
00:01:44,637 --> 00:01:45,472
CONFIDENTIAL

39
00:01:45,538 --> 00:01:48,675
<i>Most nurses in their 20's</i>
<i>do not support you.</i>

40
00:01:49,075 --> 00:01:49,909
Hey.

41
00:01:51,411 --> 00:01:53,446
Kondo's popularity is so high.

42
00:01:53,513 --> 00:01:55,048
Is his appearance the key factor?

43
00:01:56,983 --> 00:01:58,084
Never mind.

44
00:01:58,151 --> 00:01:59,953
He's an instructor.

45
00:02:00,019 --> 00:02:02,122
- He won't run for the election.
- So clumsy!

46
00:02:02,188 --> 00:02:03,189
I agree.

47
00:02:04,124 --> 00:02:06,893
And what is Kondo doing?

48
00:02:06,960 --> 00:02:09,863
Dr. Kondo has performed
an innovative operation.

49
00:02:09,929 --> 00:02:12,432
He's going to make a speech.

50
00:02:12,932 --> 00:02:15,535
Before that, may I?

51
00:02:15,602 --> 00:02:20,573
I am Hiruma, the executive
manager of surgery department.

52
00:02:20,640 --> 00:02:22,876
Nice to meet you all.
Kondo's surgery...

53
00:02:22,942 --> 00:02:25,879
was phenomenal.

54
00:02:26,779 --> 00:02:31,818
He performed the transplant
surgery simultaneously

55
00:02:32,318 --> 00:02:37,257
on two patients with organ failure,
and cured them completely.

56
00:02:37,323 --> 00:02:40,160
This is quite something.

57
00:02:41,161 --> 00:02:47,066
Dr. Kondo, your presentation
has received a good reputation.

58
00:02:47,734 --> 00:02:48,801
- Thank you.
- That is...

59
00:02:48,868 --> 00:02:51,871
Here, take a look.

60
00:02:51,938 --> 00:02:54,841
"Organ transplant
for kidney and small intestine."

61
00:02:54,908 --> 00:02:56,876
How did you come up with the idea?

62
00:02:57,477 --> 00:03:03,483
Well, there were two patients
who are relatives.

63
00:03:04,150 --> 00:03:10,190
Their blood types and
the HLA types were matched.

64
00:03:10,256 --> 00:03:14,727
- So the operations were possible.
- That's it.

65
00:03:19,399 --> 00:03:25,004
Hey, I can't wait in the lobby.
It is packed.

66
00:03:25,071 --> 00:03:27,807
I'm sorry. But wait for your turn.

67
00:03:27,874 --> 00:03:30,109
- You can be friendly.
- I'm in a hurry.

68
00:03:30,176 --> 00:03:32,779
You should not ignore me.

69
00:03:32,845 --> 00:03:33,680
What?

70
00:03:35,014 --> 00:03:36,816
- Don't you know who I am?
- Who?

71
00:03:36,883 --> 00:03:40,119
Where is Shinobu Kondo, the surgeon?

72
00:03:41,221 --> 00:03:42,255
Who?

73
00:03:43,423 --> 00:03:46,593
So many reporters were there.

74
00:03:46,659 --> 00:03:47,493
SHIGEKATSU HIRUMA
EXECUTIVE MANAGER OF SURGERY DEPT.

75
00:03:47,560 --> 00:03:49,862
Kondo, now you've become a new hero.

76
00:03:49,929 --> 00:03:51,197
Thank you.

77
00:03:51,264 --> 00:03:52,699
- Hi. How are you?
- Hello.

78
00:03:52,765 --> 00:03:53,666
Greetings.

79
00:03:53,733 --> 00:03:55,501
- Press for the 1st floor.
- Yes.

80
00:03:56,202 --> 00:04:00,707
Kondo, have you set up
a date with my daughter?

81
00:04:01,674 --> 00:04:04,544
- I haven't had time for it.
- Yeah, you're right.

82
00:04:14,554 --> 00:04:15,421
Excuse us.

83
00:04:16,522 --> 00:04:19,859
You will get more attention,

84
00:04:20,226 --> 00:04:22,295
so take care of your private life.

85
00:04:22,595 --> 00:04:23,563
Sure.

86
00:04:31,904 --> 00:04:35,408
How many people are in your family?

87
00:04:36,175 --> 00:04:38,878
My mother passed away five years ago.

88
00:04:39,445 --> 00:04:40,780
My father lives in Kamata.

89
00:04:41,147 --> 00:04:43,683
I see. Is he also a doctor?

90
00:04:44,684 --> 00:04:48,688
No. He's worked in the industrial area.

91
00:04:49,789 --> 00:04:50,690
Is he an engineer?

92
00:04:51,424 --> 00:04:52,292
Kind of.

93
00:04:52,358 --> 00:04:58,598
No way. Melon Seiko can't win.

94
00:04:58,665 --> 00:05:02,235
You don't get it.
That's why you're an amateur.

95
00:05:02,302 --> 00:05:03,202
Listen.

96
00:05:04,570 --> 00:05:06,739
- Let's go this way.
- Hey, Dr. Kondo.

97
00:05:09,776 --> 00:05:12,912
- Shinobu!
- Hold on. Who the heck are you?

98
00:05:12,979 --> 00:05:14,914
He's Dr. Kondo's father.

99
00:05:14,981 --> 00:05:16,282
What?

100
00:05:17,650 --> 00:05:19,786
Hi. I'm his father, Rokusuke.

101
00:05:19,852 --> 00:05:21,954
Oh? I see.

102
00:05:22,455 --> 00:05:26,659
I'm the executive manager
of surgery department, Hiruma.

103
00:05:26,726 --> 00:05:28,961
- Nice to meet you.
- He runs a bicycle shop.

104
00:05:29,028 --> 00:05:30,029
Bicycle shop?

105
00:05:32,565 --> 00:05:34,033
What are you doing here?

106
00:05:34,100 --> 00:05:36,302
I want you to see this.

107
00:05:36,369 --> 00:05:39,572
Look at this diagnosis.

108
00:05:39,639 --> 00:05:41,774
I don't agree with the local doctor.

109
00:05:41,841 --> 00:05:44,077
Dr. Daimon, take him
to the reception, please.

110
00:05:44,143 --> 00:05:46,446
- No way.
- Why not?

111
00:05:46,512 --> 00:05:49,282
- What about the horseracing?
- You're right...

112
00:05:49,716 --> 00:05:51,484
We have no time.

113
00:05:51,551 --> 00:05:53,353
- Shinobu.
- Let's go, Prof. Hiruma.

114
00:05:53,419 --> 00:05:54,420
What about...

115
00:05:54,487 --> 00:05:56,022
Excuse us, Mr. Kondo.

116
00:05:56,723 --> 00:05:58,024
Shinobu, hey!

117
00:05:59,058 --> 00:06:01,194
Are you my son's pupil?

118
00:06:01,260 --> 00:06:02,128
What?

119
00:06:03,296 --> 00:06:04,564
No, I'm not.

120
00:06:05,198 --> 00:06:08,301
Hey, we still should discuss the race.

121
00:06:09,669 --> 00:06:12,772
Wait. If you want to win the race,

122
00:06:13,206 --> 00:06:17,410
you should listen to me.
I'm a genius on betting.

123
00:06:18,611 --> 00:06:21,781
<i>This is a story</i>
<i>about a maverick female doctor.</i>

124
00:06:22,348 --> 00:06:26,419
- Your mother was quite beautiful.
- No, she wasn't.

125
00:06:27,387 --> 00:06:29,655
Or it wouldn't make any sense.

126
00:06:30,223 --> 00:06:32,759
<i>University hospitals lost</i>
<i>their authorities,</i>

127
00:06:32,825 --> 00:06:34,861
<i>and the doctors' hierarchy collapsed.</i>

128
00:06:35,828 --> 00:06:37,730
<i>The world of medical care</i>

129
00:06:38,264 --> 00:06:41,267
<i>has entered into the jungle law.</i>

130
00:06:41,334 --> 00:06:44,137
People over 40's definitely
support you.

131
00:06:44,203 --> 00:06:47,373
People in their 20's are
huge fans of Kondo.

132
00:06:47,440 --> 00:06:48,307
That's why.

133
00:06:49,942 --> 00:06:53,146
- You're a boy toy.
- Am I?

134
00:06:53,813 --> 00:06:58,217
<i>To save this crisis in the world of</i>
<i>medical care, a freelance doctor,</i>

135
00:06:58,651 --> 00:07:02,121
<i>in anther words,</i>
<i>a maverick doctor, appeared.</i>

136
00:07:04,590 --> 00:07:07,960
- Move that toward you.
- Yes, ma'am.

137
00:07:08,027 --> 00:07:10,363
<i>For example, this woman.</i>

138
00:07:11,631 --> 00:07:15,401
<i>She hates groups, authority,</i>
<i>and being controlled.</i>

139
00:07:16,569 --> 00:07:21,741
<i>Her medical certifications</i>
<i>and work experience are her only weapons.</i>

140
00:07:22,642 --> 00:07:24,911
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

141
00:07:25,845 --> 00:07:28,881
<i>as known as Doctor-X.</i>

142
00:07:39,025 --> 00:07:40,393
EXAMINATION REPORT

143
00:07:40,460 --> 00:07:42,061
ROKUSUKE KONDO

144
00:07:42,128 --> 00:07:43,830
DISEASE: HEPATITIS

145
00:07:44,497 --> 00:07:46,132
Dr. Kondo is pretty amazing.

146
00:07:46,199 --> 00:07:48,034
He has been offered many interviews.

147
00:07:48,100 --> 00:07:50,436
One thesis made him famous.

148
00:07:51,037 --> 00:07:52,572
You guys are exaggerating.

149
00:07:52,638 --> 00:07:57,009
It only made him famous in our field.
It's not like he won the Nobel Prize.

150
00:07:57,076 --> 00:07:58,478
I agree.

151
00:08:00,546 --> 00:08:01,214
What?

152
00:08:02,381 --> 00:08:03,182
What is it?

153
00:08:05,251 --> 00:08:06,018
It's 12:00.

154
00:08:06,586 --> 00:08:07,920
Time to get lunch.

155
00:08:09,522 --> 00:08:12,291
She's only interested in
food and surgery.

156
00:08:17,096 --> 00:08:20,933
I'm sorry that
I had to reschedule operations.

157
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:22,435
I support your success.

158
00:08:23,336 --> 00:08:25,638
It's alright.

159
00:08:26,572 --> 00:08:27,573
Thank you.

160
00:08:29,242 --> 00:08:34,347
By the way, I heard that
your father runs a bicycle shop.

161
00:08:35,581 --> 00:08:36,649
Right.

162
00:08:36,716 --> 00:08:39,051
I may ask him
to fix my wife and son's bicycles.

163
00:08:39,519 --> 00:08:41,387
My bike got a flat tire.

164
00:08:41,721 --> 00:08:43,422
- That old one?
- Not that one.

165
00:08:50,463 --> 00:08:52,431
Thanks for taking care of my father.

166
00:08:54,166 --> 00:08:57,837
His hemoglobin level is low,
and he has mild anemia.

167
00:08:57,904 --> 00:08:58,871
What?

168
00:08:59,505 --> 00:09:01,407
I'm talking about your father.

169
00:09:02,675 --> 00:09:03,910
It's just hepatitis.

170
00:09:03,976 --> 00:09:06,879
Not developed into cirrhosis,

171
00:09:06,946 --> 00:09:08,981
but the mild splenomegaly is seen.

172
00:09:09,048 --> 00:09:11,017
His hemoglobin level is okay.

173
00:09:11,484 --> 00:09:14,620
I told him not to drink too much.

174
00:09:20,526 --> 00:09:21,427
What?

175
00:09:22,194 --> 00:09:23,930
You don't like your father, do you?

176
00:09:25,865 --> 00:09:27,433
No, I don't.

177
00:09:28,434 --> 00:09:30,536
You two are so different.

178
00:09:31,470 --> 00:09:34,607
Well, he doesn't exactly
set a good example.

179
00:09:34,907 --> 00:09:35,775
Oh yeah?

180
00:09:35,841 --> 00:09:37,910
His job is like a hobby.

181
00:09:38,311 --> 00:09:40,813
He fixes flat tires for kids for free,

182
00:09:40,880 --> 00:09:43,182
even though he isn't asked to do.

183
00:09:43,249 --> 00:09:46,686
He drinks every day and gambles a lot.

184
00:09:47,620 --> 00:09:52,525
I longed to have a job
which is totally different from his.

185
00:09:54,126 --> 00:09:56,162
Doctors are also
in the service industry.

186
00:09:57,930 --> 00:10:01,100
- Know what his favorite phrase is?
- What?

187
00:10:01,867 --> 00:10:04,136
"Living for today is great."

188
00:10:06,772 --> 00:10:09,108
He has no desire to achieve anything.

189
00:10:11,010 --> 00:10:13,946
He's an example of wasting life away.

190
00:10:15,247 --> 00:10:16,215
He sounds fun to me.

191
00:10:24,123 --> 00:10:24,957
Hello?

192
00:10:25,825 --> 00:10:28,094
I'll be right there.
Excuse me.

193
00:10:29,128 --> 00:10:30,963
Just forget about my father.

194
00:10:38,971 --> 00:10:41,007
Don't waste it.

195
00:10:46,712 --> 00:10:50,016
You seem to be working tirelessly.

196
00:10:50,082 --> 00:10:52,952
KAZUYO MABUCHI
EXECUTIVE MANAGER OF INTERNAL MEDICINE

197
00:10:53,019 --> 00:10:54,120
Dr. Kondo.

198
00:10:54,186 --> 00:10:57,723
I'm sorry that I couldn't
go to Paris with you.

199
00:10:57,790 --> 00:10:59,158
It was a boring trip.

200
00:11:00,893 --> 00:11:04,764
But I found out some big news.

201
00:11:05,398 --> 00:11:06,232
Is that so?

202
00:11:08,234 --> 00:11:09,101
What is it?

203
00:11:11,537 --> 00:11:14,306
Well, I'll tell you someday.

204
00:11:22,948 --> 00:11:27,019
The color of Tokyo is
so different from that of Paris.

205
00:11:27,920 --> 00:11:31,524
You would totally enjoy Paris.

206
00:11:34,093 --> 00:11:37,063
- You didn't want me to come back?
- Of course I did.

207
00:11:41,067 --> 00:11:45,738
I saw your interview on TV.
You were something.

208
00:11:46,605 --> 00:11:47,640
Thank you.

209
00:11:48,474 --> 00:11:49,575
You've been

210
00:11:51,644 --> 00:11:55,581
hanging around Hiruma recently.

211
00:11:56,082 --> 00:11:58,150
That's not true.

212
00:12:01,220 --> 00:12:03,656
Well, excuse me.

213
00:12:05,825 --> 00:12:06,826
You

214
00:12:09,128 --> 00:12:12,064
seem to have become
content with your life.

215
00:12:15,367 --> 00:12:16,402
Thank you.

216
00:12:23,509 --> 00:12:26,412
"Living for today is great?"

217
00:12:26,479 --> 00:12:27,680
That's exactly right.

218
00:12:27,747 --> 00:12:29,482
Do you understand?

219
00:12:30,549 --> 00:12:34,019
Most doctors think the same way.

220
00:12:34,086 --> 00:12:35,087
Yeah?

221
00:12:35,421 --> 00:12:36,722
For their patients.

222
00:12:37,823 --> 00:12:38,657
That's funny.

223
00:12:39,759 --> 00:12:40,593
Reach.

224
00:12:42,461 --> 00:12:43,395
I almost win!

225
00:12:43,462 --> 00:12:48,067
His blood pressure was 116/75,
and the pulse rate was 100.

226
00:12:49,668 --> 00:12:51,804
My son's pupil, hurry to play.

227
00:12:51,871 --> 00:12:53,105
I'm not his pupil.

228
00:12:53,172 --> 00:12:54,340
- His breathing rate?
- 18.

229
00:12:54,406 --> 00:12:55,875
It is normal.

230
00:12:56,408 --> 00:12:57,710
It's safe.

231
00:12:57,777 --> 00:13:00,546
His tarsal conjunctiva
shows mild anemia.

232
00:13:01,280 --> 00:13:02,314
Chest pain?

233
00:13:02,381 --> 00:13:06,519
The chest is good, except
the tenderness on his left abdomen.

234
00:13:06,585 --> 00:13:08,554
What are you guys talking about?

235
00:13:08,621 --> 00:13:09,822
Abdominal sounds?

236
00:13:10,756 --> 00:13:13,692
- It's safe.
- The abdominal sounds was low.

237
00:13:14,226 --> 00:13:16,896
- Blood test?
- The hemoglobin level was 8.9.

238
00:13:16,962 --> 00:13:18,898
The problem is mild anemia.

239
00:13:18,964 --> 00:13:20,232
Hurry.

240
00:13:20,299 --> 00:13:21,801
Mild splenomegaly was detected.

241
00:13:21,867 --> 00:13:23,602
The pulse rate is high.

242
00:13:23,669 --> 00:13:26,806
Hemoglobin level is low
and pulse rate is high,

243
00:13:26,872 --> 00:13:29,441
- and bleeding...
- Hurry to play.

244
00:13:30,209 --> 00:13:33,179
Did you hit your tummy recently?

245
00:13:33,245 --> 00:13:35,514
- What?
- Did you?

246
00:13:38,517 --> 00:13:42,354
I fell down the stairs
a few weeks ago and hit my side.

247
00:13:42,421 --> 00:13:43,489
- Really?
- Yeah.

248
00:13:47,159 --> 00:13:49,728
Ron.

249
00:13:49,795 --> 00:13:51,597
Men-tan-pin-sanshoku-doradora!

250
00:13:52,264 --> 00:13:56,168
How beautiful! Such a rare hand!

251
00:13:56,235 --> 00:13:59,038
- You may have to be cut.
- Thanks to him.

252
00:13:59,104 --> 00:14:00,706
- Let's go.
- Where?

253
00:14:00,773 --> 00:14:02,575
- To the hospital.
- What for?

254
00:14:02,641 --> 00:14:04,043
Go to the hospital.

255
00:14:04,109 --> 00:14:05,044
Why?

256
00:14:27,066 --> 00:14:29,335
For the detailed operative approach,

257
00:14:29,401 --> 00:14:30,870
He's been featured?

258
00:14:30,936 --> 00:14:33,105
SHINOBU KONDO
TEITO UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL

259
00:14:33,172 --> 00:14:34,740
The camera is leaving me...Why?

260
00:14:35,174 --> 00:14:39,078
You also look great on TV.

261
00:14:39,144 --> 00:14:42,014
- Yes, he does.
- Thank you.

262
00:14:42,781 --> 00:14:46,785
You are not on TV at all, honey.

263
00:14:46,852 --> 00:14:49,855
Because this interview is for Kondo.

264
00:14:49,922 --> 00:14:53,259
- It doesn't matter whether I was on TV.
- Right.

265
00:14:53,325 --> 00:14:55,995
It's not a big deal.

266
00:14:57,997 --> 00:15:00,432
That was a great press conference.

267
00:15:04,136 --> 00:15:07,473
- By the way. Kondo.
- Yes?

268
00:15:07,539 --> 00:15:10,476
Would you perform surgery tomorrow?

269
00:15:11,510 --> 00:15:12,344
Sure.

270
00:15:13,245 --> 00:15:17,149
It's for Kataoka's older brother,
the democratic party's head.

271
00:15:19,218 --> 00:15:20,452
He has insulinoma.

272
00:15:22,955 --> 00:15:26,225
This is the good timing for you

273
00:15:26,625 --> 00:15:29,728
to perform surgery
on our special patient.

274
00:15:30,329 --> 00:15:31,163
Thank you so much.

275
00:15:31,230 --> 00:15:34,600
It will be helpful
to endorse you as a professor.

276
00:15:35,401 --> 00:15:37,703
A professor? Me?

277
00:15:39,004 --> 00:15:41,106
Are you going to become a professor?

278
00:15:41,173 --> 00:15:43,742
That'll be a great promotion!

279
00:15:43,809 --> 00:15:47,046
You have such a strong luck.

280
00:15:47,112 --> 00:15:52,284
Let's say, you are sitting here.

281
00:15:52,584 --> 00:15:57,589
I've been with Ebina for long time,
while I've never invited him over.

282
00:15:59,224 --> 00:16:00,359
I'm honored.

283
00:16:00,426 --> 00:16:03,896
Well, let's open Opus One of 1982.

284
00:16:04,296 --> 00:16:08,334
Not 1982. Hey, don't do that.

285
00:16:10,402 --> 00:16:12,037
- Who's calling?
- The hospital.

286
00:16:12,104 --> 00:16:14,940
You can pass it on to someone.

287
00:16:15,007 --> 00:16:15,841
Excuse me.

288
00:16:17,376 --> 00:16:18,277
Hello?

289
00:16:18,711 --> 00:16:21,313
- <i>It can be delayed splenic rupture.</i>
- What?

290
00:16:21,380 --> 00:16:22,614
This is about your father.

291
00:16:24,817 --> 00:16:27,453
No way. His hepatitis has
just progressed a bit.

292
00:16:27,519 --> 00:16:31,123
He fell down the stairs
and hit his side recently.

293
00:16:31,924 --> 00:16:35,060
Something makes
his hemoglobin level low.

294
00:16:35,127 --> 00:16:36,462
Is it splenic injury?

295
00:16:37,863 --> 00:16:40,132
A clear ruptured splenic isn't here.

296
00:16:40,199 --> 00:16:44,236
Here, clot is on the spleen.
It can start from here.

297
00:16:44,737 --> 00:16:47,539
Hello? I put him in the hospital.

298
00:16:47,606 --> 00:16:50,509
But his spleen hasn't been ruptured.

299
00:16:50,576 --> 00:16:53,278
I have no time to argue with you.

300
00:16:53,345 --> 00:16:54,213
I'll hang up.

301
00:16:54,713 --> 00:16:55,714
What?

302
00:16:57,449 --> 00:16:59,318
It'll be too late
when it gets ruptured!

303
00:17:08,994 --> 00:17:10,462
I heard a woman's voice.

304
00:17:12,631 --> 00:17:15,167
She is not a woman.

305
00:17:27,146 --> 00:17:30,115
That's good. You're a craftsman!

306
00:17:30,182 --> 00:17:34,053
But you should go back
to your room. You're a patient.

307
00:17:37,189 --> 00:17:40,793
- Is he really Dr. Kondo's father?
- Yes, he is.

308
00:17:41,593 --> 00:17:45,831
A black hen lays a white egg.

309
00:17:49,601 --> 00:17:51,136
It's almost done.

310
00:17:51,537 --> 00:17:54,106
That's great, father.

311
00:17:54,173 --> 00:17:57,109
I was going to call a specialist.

312
00:17:57,176 --> 00:18:00,145
I'm a specialist. Pay me 1,000 yen.

313
00:18:01,647 --> 00:18:03,549
You know,

314
00:18:04,016 --> 00:18:06,351
- what do you call that?
- A spoke.

315
00:18:06,418 --> 00:18:09,822
I lost two spokes,
but I didn't fix them.

316
00:18:09,888 --> 00:18:11,557
That's no good.

317
00:18:11,623 --> 00:18:16,895
Listen, every single part
exists for a reason.

318
00:18:16,962 --> 00:18:19,264
- None of them are unnecessary.
- Right.

319
00:18:19,331 --> 00:18:20,933
Take good care of things.

320
00:18:21,366 --> 00:18:23,335
If it breaks, fix it immediately.

321
00:18:23,402 --> 00:18:25,771
You've got it, my son's pupil?

322
00:18:25,838 --> 00:18:27,473
- I'm not his pupil.
- Yes, you are.

323
00:18:27,539 --> 00:18:29,675
- No, I'm not.
- I know it.

324
00:18:29,741 --> 00:18:31,510
Go back to your room.

325
00:18:32,211 --> 00:18:34,379
The urgent preoperative conference.

326
00:18:34,813 --> 00:18:38,450
The patient is male, 70,
Senkichiro Kataoka.

327
00:18:38,951 --> 00:18:41,353
Diagnosis is a solitary insulinoma.

328
00:18:42,221 --> 00:18:43,689
He is the

329
00:18:43,755 --> 00:18:49,628
most urgent patient
of executive manager Hiruma.

330
00:18:49,695 --> 00:18:51,096
The surgeon

331
00:18:53,265 --> 00:18:54,700
will be Dr. Kondo.

332
00:18:57,169 --> 00:18:58,003
Yes, sir.

333
00:18:59,771 --> 00:19:03,342
Kondo performs surgery on
the older brother of Mr. Kataoka?

334
00:19:03,775 --> 00:19:07,446
Hiruma has suddenly
made this decision.

335
00:19:10,849 --> 00:19:16,221
The operative method is the splenic
tumor enucleation by laparoscopy.

336
00:19:16,288 --> 00:19:18,590
Why did Hiruma assign Kondo?

337
00:19:18,657 --> 00:19:21,393
Pancreas diseases are
Prof. Ebina's specialty.

338
00:19:22,161 --> 00:19:23,362
Don't you get it?

339
00:19:24,763 --> 00:19:26,765
This is Prof. Hiruma's discretion.

340
00:19:26,832 --> 00:19:31,203
He's considered to reduce my burden

341
00:19:31,270 --> 00:19:35,707
because the chairperson's election
is coming soon.

342
00:19:36,108 --> 00:19:38,510
That's thoughtful.

343
00:19:39,444 --> 00:19:40,679
- Thoughtful.
- Thoughtful.

344
00:19:40,746 --> 00:19:42,414
You guys are still immature.

345
00:19:44,416 --> 00:19:45,350
Also,

346
00:19:45,817 --> 00:19:50,122
Prof. Ebina is going to
assist this operation.

347
00:19:50,989 --> 00:19:52,124
- Assist?
- Yes.

348
00:19:52,758 --> 00:19:54,826
- This is Executive Manager's order.
- Yes.

349
00:19:55,594 --> 00:19:56,428
That's right.

350
00:19:59,031 --> 00:19:59,865
Yes, sir.

351
00:20:04,203 --> 00:20:05,270
Hold on.

352
00:20:06,805 --> 00:20:09,641
We have a more urgent patient.

353
00:20:09,708 --> 00:20:11,043
How rude you are!

354
00:20:11,109 --> 00:20:14,279
Dr. Kondo's father needs
pancreas surgery now.

355
00:20:15,314 --> 00:20:17,249
Dr. Daimon, I told you...

356
00:20:17,316 --> 00:20:19,718
Splenic rupture,
a type 1b with hematoma.

357
00:20:19,785 --> 00:20:22,554
It can be
the delayed splenic rupture.

358
00:20:22,621 --> 00:20:25,290
Even if it gets ruptured,

359
00:20:25,357 --> 00:20:27,859
you can simply remove the pancreas.

360
00:20:27,926 --> 00:20:30,796
- Simply?
- How can you assume rupture?

361
00:20:30,862 --> 00:20:33,265
The surgery has to be done
before the rupture.

362
00:20:33,332 --> 00:20:36,969
If it get ruptured, it'd be
difficult to preserve the spleen.

363
00:20:37,035 --> 00:20:38,870
To preserve the spleen?

364
00:20:39,404 --> 00:20:41,673
Removal is a typical treatment.

365
00:20:42,274 --> 00:20:44,142
And there's no threat to his life.

366
00:20:44,476 --> 00:20:46,578
Don't you know that, freelancer?

367
00:20:49,581 --> 00:20:52,884
Excuse me.
Rokusuke Kondo collapsed suddenly.

368
00:21:04,596 --> 00:21:06,164
Do you recognize me?

369
00:21:06,231 --> 00:21:08,100
He said a pain on his abdominal.

370
00:21:08,166 --> 00:21:09,468
- Do the CT-scan now.
- Yes.

371
00:21:13,238 --> 00:21:16,174
His spleen gets ruptured.
Perform urgent surgery.

372
00:21:16,241 --> 00:21:18,443
He wants to tell you something.

373
00:21:20,545 --> 00:21:25,717
- We're going to perform surgery.
- It hurts. I don't want you to do that.

374
00:21:26,652 --> 00:21:31,189
- Shinobu. I want you to do that.
- Dad...

375
00:21:33,392 --> 00:21:36,261
Dr. Kondo, what are you doing?

376
00:21:38,597 --> 00:21:41,933
Everybody is waiting for you.
Come and greet them.

377
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:44,536
Sure. Dr. Daimon, please.

378
00:21:44,603 --> 00:21:47,973
I don't want your pupil
to do that on me.

379
00:21:48,040 --> 00:21:49,775
- Like I said...
- Don't worry.

380
00:21:49,841 --> 00:21:52,311
Removal of spleen is
an easy operation.

381
00:21:54,646 --> 00:21:55,714
Thanks, Dr. Daimon.

382
00:21:56,448 --> 00:22:00,018
Shinobu! I don't want
your pupil to do that!

383
00:22:00,085 --> 00:22:01,186
I'm not his pupil.

384
00:22:02,220 --> 00:22:03,689
And I never fail.

385
00:22:12,197 --> 00:22:15,901
This is Mr. Yuhara from
the Democratic Party of Japan.

386
00:22:15,967 --> 00:22:17,069
Good to meet you.

387
00:22:17,135 --> 00:22:19,871
That is Mr. Mitsuya.

388
00:22:20,238 --> 00:22:21,239
An honor to meet you.

389
00:22:23,041 --> 00:22:25,377
Oh, hi.

390
00:22:26,078 --> 00:22:28,413
Well, well, well.

391
00:22:29,381 --> 00:22:31,750
Thanks for coming, the head of
the Democratic Party.

392
00:22:31,817 --> 00:22:33,618
- Take care of my big brother.
- Sure.

393
00:22:33,685 --> 00:22:37,823
We're honored to have the opportunity

394
00:22:37,889 --> 00:22:40,826
to perform surgery on your brother.

395
00:22:40,892 --> 00:22:42,694
We are very honored.

396
00:22:43,462 --> 00:22:44,963
So, are you the surgeon?

397
00:22:45,030 --> 00:22:46,164
Yes, sir.

398
00:22:46,231 --> 00:22:49,801
Though Dr. Kondo is young,
his skill is superb.

399
00:22:49,868 --> 00:22:50,936
You're in good hands.

400
00:22:51,837 --> 00:22:56,041
Dr. Ebina is going to assist him.

401
00:22:56,108 --> 00:22:58,143
Our expert will do this operation.

402
00:22:59,244 --> 00:23:00,479
- Right?
- Yes sir.

403
00:23:00,779 --> 00:23:03,415
- You don't sound energetic.
- Yes, sir.

404
00:23:12,023 --> 00:23:14,826
The catecholamine improve
the blood pressure to 70.

405
00:23:15,761 --> 00:23:17,729
Dr. Daimon will proceed to

406
00:23:17,796 --> 00:23:19,564
- remove the spleen...
- I won't do that.

407
00:23:21,333 --> 00:23:23,001
I won't remove the spleen.

408
00:23:23,468 --> 00:23:25,704
- Change the operative method.
- You've got it.

409
00:23:25,771 --> 00:23:26,805
What?

410
00:23:30,342 --> 00:23:33,545
Do you understand
how special this surgery is?

411
00:23:35,113 --> 00:23:36,348
You've been chosen.

412
00:23:37,916 --> 00:23:41,086
This operation is mine
under a normal circumstance.

413
00:23:41,553 --> 00:23:43,321
I pass it onto you so you can grow.

414
00:23:44,823 --> 00:23:47,692
Anyway, do your best.

415
00:23:50,295 --> 00:23:51,163
Hurry.

416
00:23:57,369 --> 00:23:58,270
What is it?

417
00:24:00,272 --> 00:24:01,306
Prof. Ebina.

418
00:24:12,517 --> 00:24:14,586
What a flexible operative method.

419
00:24:14,653 --> 00:24:16,388
That's like Kondo.

420
00:24:17,489 --> 00:24:19,458
That old dude...I mean...

421
00:24:22,027 --> 00:24:26,298
Ebina wouldn't have
thought of that approach.

422
00:24:26,798 --> 00:24:28,033
Sure not.

423
00:24:28,633 --> 00:24:30,502
Prof. Ebina is over...

424
00:24:33,905 --> 00:24:34,906
What?

425
00:24:37,542 --> 00:24:38,510
That's Prof. Ebina.

426
00:24:40,545 --> 00:24:41,780
Not Kondo.

427
00:24:45,217 --> 00:24:46,084
What's going on?

428
00:24:49,921 --> 00:24:54,259
We perform splenic tumor
enucleation by laparoscopy.

429
00:24:55,694 --> 00:24:57,128
I'll appreciate your support.

430
00:24:57,195 --> 00:24:58,864
Thank you, sir.

431
00:25:03,034 --> 00:25:03,935
- Scalpel.
- Yes.

432
00:25:08,707 --> 00:25:09,541
- Forceps.
- Here.

433
00:25:11,810 --> 00:25:15,447
What happened to Kondo?

434
00:25:20,151 --> 00:25:21,219
Dr. Kondo.

435
00:25:21,653 --> 00:25:24,789
I've removed the damaged field.
Do astriction.

436
00:25:24,856 --> 00:25:25,957
Yes, ma'am.

437
00:25:27,225 --> 00:25:28,059
Let me do it.

438
00:25:28,960 --> 00:25:29,794
No way.

439
00:25:30,762 --> 00:25:31,630
Please.

440
00:25:44,776 --> 00:25:48,813
You are not removing total spleen?

441
00:25:48,880 --> 00:25:50,215
I'm not doing it.

442
00:25:50,815 --> 00:25:52,384
I'm doing partial splenectomy.

443
00:25:52,450 --> 00:25:54,252
I removed the damaged field,

444
00:25:54,319 --> 00:25:57,422
and I repaired the splenic vessels
for preserved area.

445
00:25:57,489 --> 00:26:00,458
Repair the vessels
and preserve partial spleen?

446
00:26:01,693 --> 00:26:03,962
Too complex. Simply remove them all.

447
00:26:04,029 --> 00:26:05,230
Why?

448
00:26:05,597 --> 00:26:07,299
Spleen is not important...

449
00:26:07,365 --> 00:26:08,934
Every organ has a meaning.

450
00:26:10,602 --> 00:26:13,405
Every single part
of our body is important.

451
00:26:15,774 --> 00:26:18,543
What are you doing?
Are we having a discussion now?

452
00:26:21,913 --> 00:26:24,349
I've never done spleen-sparing.

453
00:26:24,416 --> 00:26:26,718
I'll teach you, so watch me. Move.

454
00:26:28,253 --> 00:26:30,488
Let's resume. Monopolar.

455
00:26:32,424 --> 00:26:34,559
Repair arteries
of splenic trabecula.

456
00:26:34,626 --> 00:26:37,162
First assistant, shut down its root.

457
00:26:37,228 --> 00:26:39,631
- Give me the loupe.
- Yes, sir.

458
00:26:39,698 --> 00:26:40,665
- Forceps.
- Yes.

459
00:26:49,274 --> 00:26:51,309
Reinforce the suture site.

460
00:26:51,376 --> 00:26:52,544
Yes. Pledget.

461
00:27:10,595 --> 00:27:12,864
- What is the total blood loss?
- 60cc.

462
00:27:13,298 --> 00:27:15,667
All right. It's done.

463
00:27:18,203 --> 00:27:20,305
Great job.

464
00:27:23,108 --> 00:27:24,876
Thank you, sir.

465
00:27:41,926 --> 00:27:43,094
Ebina...

466
00:28:02,080 --> 00:28:03,214
Why did you do this?

467
00:28:03,982 --> 00:28:06,618
Spleen tissue is easy
to get damaged.

468
00:28:06,685 --> 00:28:10,121
Why did you take this risk,
instead of removal?

469
00:28:10,455 --> 00:28:13,391
Your father's hepatitis
is caused by alcohol.

470
00:28:14,459 --> 00:28:15,326
So?

471
00:28:15,694 --> 00:28:18,830
It is the advanced condition
of fatty liver,

472
00:28:18,897 --> 00:28:21,232
and likely to cause a heart attack.

473
00:28:22,767 --> 00:28:24,335
Dr. Daimon, what's your point?

474
00:28:24,402 --> 00:28:26,905
Mononuclear cells in the spleen

475
00:28:26,971 --> 00:28:30,208
help with cardiac recovery
after a heart attack.

476
00:28:30,809 --> 00:28:32,844
- Cardiac?
- You think spleen is unnecessary.

477
00:28:32,911 --> 00:28:34,412
If you remove it, though,

478
00:28:34,479 --> 00:28:38,983
the chance of your father's recovery
would be greatly reduced

479
00:28:39,050 --> 00:28:42,020
if he ever has a heart attack.

480
00:28:43,788 --> 00:28:45,990
Overall, the probability of
your father's death

481
00:28:46,057 --> 00:28:49,527
would be higher in the future.

482
00:28:51,763 --> 00:28:56,201
If you want him to live longer,
you should preserve his spleen.

483
00:28:57,936 --> 00:29:00,205
Mr. Kondo, it's done.

484
00:29:02,440 --> 00:29:07,512
"Living for today is great.
Living for tomorrow will be better."

485
00:29:09,614 --> 00:29:11,216
Right?

486
00:29:26,664 --> 00:29:28,500
What were you thinking?

487
00:29:28,900 --> 00:29:29,868
I'm very sorry.

488
00:29:33,738 --> 00:29:37,275
I'm so disappointed in you.

489
00:29:41,613 --> 00:29:46,651
You do understand what you've done.

490
00:29:49,254 --> 00:29:50,088
Yes, sir.

491
00:29:51,589 --> 00:29:52,557
Affection?

492
00:29:54,592 --> 00:29:58,596
Affection for your father?

493
00:30:01,533 --> 00:30:06,237
You can't climb up
this mountain of your career.

494
00:30:07,472 --> 00:30:10,308
You're such a shallow man.

495
00:30:13,211 --> 00:30:18,082
I've set up your career path.

496
00:30:21,052 --> 00:30:23,688
Right before your promotion,

497
00:30:26,591 --> 00:30:28,359
you stepped down voluntarily.

498
00:30:30,328 --> 00:30:34,365
Forget about my daughter as well.

499
00:30:38,036 --> 00:30:40,038
I don't need tea.

500
00:31:00,558 --> 00:31:05,096
I made a reservation at Omiya Sukiyabashi
in the main building at five.

501
00:31:06,064 --> 00:31:08,199
Omiya Sukiyabashi at 5:00?

502
00:31:08,266 --> 00:31:10,835
I see. Thanks.

503
00:31:13,771 --> 00:31:15,039
It seems like...

504
00:31:15,673 --> 00:31:17,709
I have to endorse Ebina

505
00:31:19,344 --> 00:31:22,146
for the chairperson election.

506
00:31:23,481 --> 00:31:27,886
Ebina...

507
00:31:28,686 --> 00:31:31,256
- You did it, Prof. Ebina!
- Great job!

508
00:31:32,123 --> 00:31:33,291
Congrats!

509
00:31:33,625 --> 00:31:35,560
I had to do it because

510
00:31:35,627 --> 00:31:38,196
Kondo asked me to switch all of a sudden.

511
00:31:38,263 --> 00:31:41,866
He just realized it was your surgery.

512
00:31:41,933 --> 00:31:44,402
- He knew it.
- I wonder.

513
00:31:46,371 --> 00:31:50,642
Now your popularity rate will go up.

514
00:31:50,708 --> 00:31:52,143
- Oh yeah?
- Of course.

515
00:31:52,844 --> 00:31:54,913
Tamao,

516
00:31:54,979 --> 00:31:59,851
Hiruma's secretary made a reservation
at Omiya Sukiyabashi at five.

517
00:32:00,585 --> 00:32:04,856
Omiya Sukiyabashi? That expensive
teppan grill restaurant?

518
00:32:04,923 --> 00:32:05,823
Right.

519
00:32:06,791 --> 00:32:09,694
Only important people
are allowed to visit there.

520
00:32:09,761 --> 00:32:13,498
In the main building?
Not the reasonable annex?

521
00:32:13,932 --> 00:32:14,832
The main building.

522
00:32:17,168 --> 00:32:19,270
You'll be called.

523
00:32:19,938 --> 00:32:22,874
At five? What time is it now?

524
00:32:23,474 --> 00:32:24,575
It's 3:30.

525
00:32:25,677 --> 00:32:26,945
Prof. Ebina.

526
00:32:27,979 --> 00:32:31,416
Omiya Sukiyabashi in the main building.

527
00:32:33,785 --> 00:32:34,752
I'm getting nervous.

528
00:32:35,720 --> 00:32:36,587
How do you feel?

529
00:32:38,990 --> 00:32:41,059
What's wrong? Any pain?

530
00:32:48,800 --> 00:32:52,370
I thought you had an important operation.

531
00:32:54,872 --> 00:32:55,707
Yeah.

532
00:32:59,777 --> 00:33:04,782
Why didn't you take
the important one, instead of mine?

533
00:33:05,450 --> 00:33:09,420
You could have gotten promoted.

534
00:33:11,022 --> 00:33:12,957
Because I care about you.

535
00:33:16,627 --> 00:33:18,296
You're lying.

536
00:33:19,497 --> 00:33:22,600
You got scared
right before the surgery.

537
00:33:23,468 --> 00:33:29,374
Geez. You've been the same
since you were a kid.

538
00:33:32,377 --> 00:33:33,611
In the future,

539
00:33:35,880 --> 00:33:38,549
you'll have to compete with

540
00:33:40,118 --> 00:33:43,021
four-year-old thoroughbred horses

541
00:33:44,222 --> 00:33:47,792
or great horses from famous stables.

542
00:33:49,594 --> 00:33:50,628
What do you do?

543
00:33:56,267 --> 00:34:00,571
A new horse from an unknown stable

544
00:34:01,773 --> 00:34:03,441
should not hesitate.

545
00:34:06,377 --> 00:34:07,845
My life is not a gamble.

546
00:34:11,015 --> 00:34:13,184
Of course, it is.

547
00:34:14,619 --> 00:34:16,687
Life is a gamble.

548
00:34:16,754 --> 00:34:22,660
Unlike me, you were born
with a winning ticket.

549
00:34:22,994 --> 00:34:24,962
Don't worry about me.

550
00:34:25,029 --> 00:34:26,063
Look,

551
00:34:27,198 --> 00:34:32,003
do not waste your ticket.

552
00:34:32,770 --> 00:34:33,938
Hold it tight.

553
00:34:34,572 --> 00:34:36,808
You've got to redeem it.

554
00:34:44,782 --> 00:34:48,386
Even that Oguricap started
his career from nothing.

555
00:34:51,355 --> 00:34:52,523
You hear me?

556
00:34:57,528 --> 00:34:59,730
Everything is too late.

557
00:35:06,838 --> 00:35:11,209
I am done.

558
00:35:11,275 --> 00:35:13,611
Omiya Sukiyabashi.

559
00:35:13,678 --> 00:35:16,547
You'll received the phone call.

560
00:35:16,614 --> 00:35:19,417
Probably his important people
will be waiting.

561
00:35:19,951 --> 00:35:24,122
Then you'll be introduce
as his successor.

562
00:35:24,188 --> 00:35:25,022
You'll score.

563
00:35:26,057 --> 00:35:30,695
You may not be able to eat beef
because you're too nervous.

564
00:35:31,329 --> 00:35:32,964
It won't happen.

565
00:35:35,533 --> 00:35:36,434
What?

566
00:35:37,535 --> 00:35:39,003
Say what you want to say.

567
00:35:39,070 --> 00:35:40,371
Nothing.

568
00:35:41,973 --> 00:35:43,307
It's time for me to go home.

569
00:35:50,815 --> 00:35:54,886
- Is the reservation at five?
- Yes. It's five.

570
00:35:56,220 --> 00:35:59,857
- Important people are always late.
- Right.

571
00:36:03,961 --> 00:36:08,699
Oh my. Three minutes
have passed since five.

572
00:36:15,006 --> 00:36:16,374
This is a melon.

573
00:36:16,440 --> 00:36:19,977
I know it. Then the bill, right?

574
00:36:20,044 --> 00:36:22,380
- Here it is.
- I knew it.

575
00:36:25,917 --> 00:36:28,553
Since he is the father of Kondo,

576
00:36:28,619 --> 00:36:31,656
I treated him with special care.

577
00:36:31,722 --> 00:36:33,824
But it wound up being wasted.

578
00:36:34,392 --> 00:36:36,460
I have no idea what you mean.

579
00:36:36,527 --> 00:36:38,763
But our Daimon performed surgery.

580
00:36:38,829 --> 00:36:40,164
It was unnecessary.

581
00:36:40,231 --> 00:36:42,233
Still, I must charge you.

582
00:36:42,300 --> 00:36:45,102
Is that so? You will charge me.

583
00:36:46,504 --> 00:36:49,540
Then tell me how much.

584
00:36:51,042 --> 00:36:53,010
Oh my God!

585
00:36:53,611 --> 00:36:55,046
What a surprise!

586
00:36:55,112 --> 00:36:58,583
Get out. I'm in a bad mood.

587
00:36:58,649 --> 00:37:01,819
I'm very sorry to hear that.

588
00:37:04,755 --> 00:37:06,724
Who is it? I'm going home.

589
00:37:06,791 --> 00:37:09,260
Excuse me.

590
00:37:09,327 --> 00:37:11,963
Hi.

591
00:37:12,029 --> 00:37:14,932
Executive manager of internal
medicine department, Mabuchi.

592
00:37:16,367 --> 00:37:19,136
- Oh.
- Long time no see.

593
00:37:21,038 --> 00:37:24,609
Executive Manager Mabuchi,
what brought you here?

594
00:37:25,443 --> 00:37:26,277
Well.

595
00:37:27,311 --> 00:37:31,082
It's rare to see you two together.

596
00:37:31,148 --> 00:37:34,685
Excuse me. Wish me luck.

597
00:37:40,925 --> 00:37:44,061
Kazuyo, how can I help you?

598
00:37:44,629 --> 00:37:49,200
I've been greeting people
all afternoon.

599
00:37:49,267 --> 00:37:50,568
Greeting people?

600
00:37:50,635 --> 00:37:55,806
I thought it'd be fine
to visit you in the end.

601
00:37:55,873 --> 00:37:56,974
In the end?

602
00:37:57,041 --> 00:37:59,877
- It's already this hour?
- I guess so.

603
00:37:59,944 --> 00:38:01,646
- Come in.
- What?

604
00:38:09,153 --> 00:38:12,390
Hello. Good to see you.

605
00:38:13,457 --> 00:38:14,592
What's going on here?

606
00:38:15,626 --> 00:38:19,530
Did you forget him?

607
00:38:20,264 --> 00:38:22,266
Of course not.

608
00:38:22,333 --> 00:38:25,036
Sorry for being a stranger.

609
00:38:25,903 --> 00:38:30,341
I used to work at
your 2nd surgery department. Takano.

610
00:38:30,408 --> 00:38:33,678
I know. I know.

611
00:38:34,679 --> 00:38:39,050
You look well. You must be
happy in your home town.

612
00:38:39,116 --> 00:38:41,719
What would you guys want me to do?

613
00:38:41,786 --> 00:38:45,323
I brought Prof. Takano back here.

614
00:38:46,023 --> 00:38:48,659
He will run for the

615
00:38:48,726 --> 00:38:50,761
- next chairperson's election.
- What?

616
00:38:50,828 --> 00:38:52,730
We're here to report this to you.

617
00:38:56,467 --> 00:38:57,468
Wait a minute.

618
00:38:58,069 --> 00:39:03,841
I ordered Mr. Takano
to relocate to Kanazawa...

619
00:39:03,908 --> 00:39:06,610
Yes. You sent me away

620
00:39:07,678 --> 00:39:09,013
at that time.

621
00:39:09,080 --> 00:39:11,082
Takano,

622
00:39:11,148 --> 00:39:14,819
I order you to transfer
to our 18th branch in Kanazawa.

623
00:39:16,787 --> 00:39:17,888
At that time...

624
00:39:17,955 --> 00:39:20,591
Didn't you know that his thesis

625
00:39:21,158 --> 00:39:27,398
was nominated
for the Kluivert Award in Paris?

626
00:39:27,465 --> 00:39:29,200
Kluivert Award?

627
00:39:29,266 --> 00:39:32,470
My research project has finally
been recognized.

628
00:39:33,838 --> 00:39:35,072
Thanks to you.

629
00:39:37,508 --> 00:39:41,045
He'll run for the election with
my endorsement.

630
00:39:42,179 --> 00:39:43,080
Please keep in mind.

631
00:39:48,352 --> 00:39:49,353
Oh yeah.

632
00:39:49,754 --> 00:39:55,826
I heard you've endorsed Ebina
for the next election.

633
00:39:57,895 --> 00:40:01,899
He's like my pupil.

634
00:40:02,733 --> 00:40:06,837
Let's compete fair and square.

635
00:40:08,906 --> 00:40:09,874
I'm afraid

636
00:40:11,776 --> 00:40:13,310
if it's going to be one-side game.

637
00:40:23,254 --> 00:40:26,724
Don't laugh.

638
00:40:30,995 --> 00:40:32,763
It's scary.

639
00:40:35,599 --> 00:40:38,302
Wish me luck.

640
00:40:41,806 --> 00:40:43,274
I'm starving.

641
00:40:45,075 --> 00:40:48,746
You still play in some extra races.

642
00:40:49,046 --> 00:40:50,214
I'm in a good condition.

643
00:40:51,215 --> 00:40:53,784
You bought a new horse.

644
00:40:57,521 --> 00:40:58,789
Kind of.

645
00:40:59,757 --> 00:41:00,591
A horse?

646
00:41:01,859 --> 00:41:04,028
This is Dr. Michiko Daimon.

647
00:41:05,296 --> 00:41:08,766
I heard about you.
You're a part-time doctor.

648
00:41:08,833 --> 00:41:10,601
I'm a freelance surgeon.

649
00:41:13,170 --> 00:41:14,972
What do you mean by a horse?

650
00:41:24,782 --> 00:41:26,784
OMIYA SUKIYABASHI
MAIN BUILDING

651
00:41:37,828 --> 00:41:39,430
- Executive Manager Hiruma,
- Yes

652
00:41:40,030 --> 00:41:44,702
I expected
to see your successor tonight.

653
00:41:45,202 --> 00:41:46,370
Yeah...

654
00:41:50,774 --> 00:41:55,279
We will introduce him
when the time comes.

655
00:41:55,346 --> 00:41:59,250
We appreciate your patronage.

656
00:42:02,620 --> 00:42:06,290
Hiruma, Dr. Ebina is late.

657
00:42:23,240 --> 00:42:25,643
I was told to come here
as soon as possible.

658
00:42:27,478 --> 00:42:29,213
Sit down.

659
00:42:33,717 --> 00:42:34,685
What's this all about?

660
00:42:34,752 --> 00:42:40,958
You seem to have better luck
than I expected.

661
00:42:42,326 --> 00:42:44,828
Still, this is your life.

662
00:42:46,497 --> 00:42:50,067
You must have your own thought.

663
00:42:51,902 --> 00:42:53,537
You decide

664
00:42:54,605 --> 00:42:57,641
whether you sit down on this chair,

665
00:43:00,411 --> 00:43:01,612
or turn around and leave.

666
00:43:10,087 --> 00:43:12,056
All gentlemen are starving.

667
00:43:14,158 --> 00:43:15,392
So, hurry.

668
00:43:46,490 --> 00:43:52,062
From now on, do not go against me.

669
00:43:53,998 --> 00:43:55,499
Professor Kondo.

670
00:44:00,971 --> 00:44:01,805
Yes sir.

671
00:44:08,479 --> 00:44:11,382
That beef tastes great with salt.

672
00:44:12,583 --> 00:44:13,550
Yes sir.

673
00:44:19,490 --> 00:44:20,324
Isn't it good?

674
00:44:20,391 --> 00:44:22,626
Here, the beef over rice bowl.

675
00:44:25,329 --> 00:44:28,432
I wonder why
so many doctors love beef.

676
00:44:29,967 --> 00:44:32,803
The chairperson's election is
coming soon.

677
00:44:33,470 --> 00:44:35,439
It has nothing to do with me.

678
00:44:35,973 --> 00:44:38,409
Karasumaru, the office manager?

679
00:44:38,475 --> 00:44:40,944
He asked me

680
00:44:41,345 --> 00:44:45,015
who would be the best chairperson.

681
00:44:45,649 --> 00:44:48,452
- I recommended you.
- Are you crazy?

682
00:44:48,519 --> 00:44:50,554
- He said the same thing.
- Of course.

683
00:44:50,621 --> 00:44:53,724
I just had a dream.

684
00:44:53,791 --> 00:44:57,327
If you become a chairperson,
everything would be so interesting.

685
00:44:58,362 --> 00:45:02,433
You're so wrong. If you don't eat that,
I will take it.

686
00:45:05,369 --> 00:45:08,372
You'll promote Dr. Kondo
to a professor,

687
00:45:08,906 --> 00:45:12,009
and make him run for the election?

688
00:45:12,576 --> 00:45:15,512
Karasumaru, this is a gamble.

689
00:45:17,514 --> 00:45:18,482
Excuse me.

690
00:45:20,651 --> 00:45:21,919
You're young.

691
00:45:21,985 --> 00:45:24,388
I'm sure you've decided correctly.

692
00:45:25,389 --> 00:45:27,157
That's like you.

693
00:45:33,731 --> 00:45:36,133
Let me advice you one thing.

694
00:45:37,000 --> 00:45:42,239
Whatever you think,
you'll get involved with them.

695
00:45:42,573 --> 00:45:46,243
I can smell cash.
Can't wait to see it.

696
00:45:47,411 --> 00:45:50,514
Can I have one more beef plate?

697
00:45:50,581 --> 00:45:51,849
Sure. Thanks!

698
00:45:52,616 --> 00:45:54,685
For example, this woman.

699
00:46:09,800 --> 00:46:11,401
Thanks for making rounds.

700
00:46:21,145 --> 00:46:22,079
Good morning.

701
00:46:23,847 --> 00:46:27,551
<i>She hates groups, authority,</i>
<i>and being controlled.</i>

702
00:46:27,951 --> 00:46:29,753
We had teppan beef last night.

703
00:46:32,256 --> 00:46:37,394
<i>Her medical certifications</i>
<i>and work experience are her only weapons.</i>

704
00:46:38,228 --> 00:46:39,663
Hey, pretty girl.

705
00:46:40,931 --> 00:46:43,133
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

706
00:46:45,035 --> 00:46:47,571
He smells like garlic.

707
00:46:47,638 --> 00:46:50,307
<i>Also known as Doctor-X.</i>

708
00:46:52,509 --> 00:46:54,478
Let's set the record straight.

709
00:46:54,545 --> 00:46:56,713
No cancers that you can't remove.

710
00:46:56,780 --> 00:46:59,449
- Which one is leading?
- I will cure you 100%.

711
00:46:59,516 --> 00:47:01,051
Be on my side?

712
00:47:01,118 --> 00:47:03,921
Our surgery got stolen!

713
00:47:03,987 --> 00:47:05,722
I got fired. Good bye.

714
00:47:05,789 --> 00:47:07,391
Don't underestimate surgery!
